1
00:00:00,250 --> 00:00:02,940
Humanity recorded the sound of touching our Sun.

2
00:00:03,680 --> 00:00:07,830
In 2021, Parker Solar Probe plunged into the solar corona.

3
00:00:07,870 --> 00:00:10,440
Temperatures hit two million degrees Fahrenheit.

4
00:00:10,530 --> 00:00:12,940
Pause. Sound cannot travel through a vacuum.

5
00:00:13,570 --> 00:00:15,870
How did sensors capture actual noise?

6
00:00:16,230 --> 00:00:19,770
Hypervelocity dust grains smashed into the probe at high speeds.

7
00:00:20,430 --> 00:00:23,800
Each collision vaporized metal, creating tiny plasma explosions.

8
00:00:23,850 --> 00:00:27,230
Instruments recorded those plasma shocks as acoustic soundwaves.

9
00:00:27,280 --> 00:00:31,330
You are hearing dust disintegrating at three hundred thousand miles per hour.

10
00:00:32,250 --> 00:00:33,460
And that is how...
